# alfred runtime identity (canonical, fixed): user alfred UID 107,
# primary group alfred GID 107. Required by the shipped service units
# (alfred.service User=alfred, alfred.initd command_user alfred:alfred).
# The daemon retains only CAP_NET_ADMIN/CAP_NET_RAW across its setuid
# drop (file caps on the binary for OpenRC, ambient caps for systemd).
# UID 104 was claimed first and refused at publication: the base seed
# reserves 104 for dhcpcd (accounts.tsv), so alfred takes adjacent
# free 107 (verified against TSV, tree fragments, and the reservation
# ledger). UID 107 sits in the preferred 0..199 packaged range - never
# reuse it for another identity. No state directory: the unix socket
# lives under /var/run/alfred, provided by tmpfiles.d (systemd) and
# checkpath (OpenRC) with this identity.
user alfred 107 alfred /var/empty /sbin/nologin
group alfred 107
